    {
      "id": "tax-fork",
      "title": "Pressure & Intelligence",
      "playstyle": "Use Raiders, Skirmishers, Scouts and Archers to make several different kinds of pressure visible at once: taxes, suppression, prepared-card attacks and hidden-information leverage.",
      "hypothesis": "Does denial stay interactive when the opponent is choosing among several small problems rather than repeatedly hitting one lock effect?",
      "combo_notes": [
        "Iron Boars and Aradai attack future attachment costs, while Red Duelists and Ilyri care about the opposing formation directly across from them.",
        "River Raiders turn existing Exhaustion into pressure instead of requiring a one-shot trigger; Seven Black Ships and Salt-Road Fleet give the Raider package other plans when nothing is Exhausted.",
        "Thornbow Hunters, Lantern Scouts, Lysa and The Scouts Had Warned Them make hidden Stratagem information actionable.",
        "Serai plus the Archer Narratives and A Volley Before Dawn creates a parallel Strength-control line, so the deck is not forced to win only through taxation."
      ],
